## GRADING (binding, tier 2; capability decides)
*Blocker:* a path beyond the three, or the counts file touched in any way; a code byte changed in `test-server.js`; a test added, removed or renamed; an added `.skip/.only/.todo/.each`, timer or `jest.mock`; non-ASCII, a secret, a person's name or an id token in an added line or the message; `DIALS = 0`, `1` or `63` green at the head, or red at a cell but E3 (the control is not independent of `DIALS`); a head run leaving an own directory of the three prefixes in a seat-owned TMPDIR (the RD-961 fix does not work), or an `afterAll` that removes a sibling it did not make (by prefix or glob), or that removes a directory a running cell still needs (a red cell); a conflict merging with new main in any path; the whole verify red at the head or at the merge result per Rule S below, or a measured pair not equal to that tree's committed pair. *Major:* a builder claim your numbers contradict (the base matrix, the head matrix, the Mac plant's colours, the TMPDIR counts, `5369/322`); a comment sentence your Mac measurement contradicts, or one that still says E2/E3 can turn red only on Linux; the delivered diff beyond the commission's closed set in anything but a true comment; an orphan dialer that makes a removed directory reappear. *Minor:* a comment sentence that is false but not about this Mac, or the E3 header reading as self-contradicting (C3(d)); a TMPDIR run where the B cell count and the guard counts disagree by an explainable amount; a message sentence your transcript contradicts (Major if it hides a behaviour change). *Note:* the two-line comment beyond the commission when true; Linux not run; the hosted Build and CodeQL on the PR head and on main after the merge NOT run; node 26 and macOS against Node 24 and `ubuntu-latest`; `home-containment` directories still left; the project's "never `rm` a variable path" line against the ticket and the precedents (C4); a lock wait; the builder's STATUS typo. **Rule S for a red you did not plant:** re-run it ALONE 3 times; fails alone at a branch tree at least once of 3 AND passes 3 of 3 at the base = Blocker; every other case is a Note with its counts (a whole-suite load timeout is a Note; the base run is the arbiter), except the `rd913` clause of C6. **GO** = every step measured with controls, nothing above Note; **GO WITH FINDINGS** = Minor and Note only; **NO GO** on any Blocker or Major, with class, "round 1 of 2", the fix shape in prose and that a second NO GO on this class ends it. Any required heavy job NOT RUN at the hard stop: the verdict carries `(conditional: <job> not run)`; no grade is written to fit the hour.

